#: ../../source/worker-rpc_README.md:4
msgid "What is it?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/worker-rpc_README.md:6
msgid ""
"This package provides a simple RPC mechanism on top of any transport that"
" transfers JSON data. It was initially conceived to provide communication"
" with web workers (and as such supports transferables), but it can be "
"used on top of many other different transport channels, i.e. "
"`postMessage` between frames, websockets via `socket.io` or JSON encoded "
"messages over pipes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/worker-rpc_README.md:12
msgid "How to use it?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/worker-rpc_README.md:14
msgid "Installation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/worker-rpc_README.md:16
msgid "You can install the library into your project via npm"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/worker-rpc_README.md:20
msgid ""
"The library is written in Typescript and will work in any environment "
"that supports ES5 and ES6-style promises (either native or through a "
"shim). No external typings are required for using this library with "
"Typescript (version >= 2)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/worker-rpc_README.md:24
msgid "Web worker example"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/worker-rpc_README.md:26
msgid ""
"In this example, we use the library to set up communication with a web "
"worker."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/worker-rpc_README.md:28
msgid "Web worker"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/worker-rpc_README.md:40
msgid ""
"The RPC provider is initialized with a function that dispatches a "
"message. This function will receive an opaque message object as first "
"argument, and a list of transferables as second argument. This allows to "
"leverage transfer of ownership instead of copying between worker and host"
" page."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/worker-rpc_README.md:45
msgid ""
"On incoming messages, `dispatch` is called on the RPC provider in order "
"to handle the message."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/worker-rpc_README.md:48
msgid ""
"Each registered RPC handler is identified by a message ID (`add` in this "
"example) and has a handler function that receives the message object and "
"can return a result either as an immediate value or as a promise."
msgstr ""

